# - Wikipedia, Bouyon soca article (opened 2026-10-20): fusion of Dominica bouyon and Trinidad soca, cultural origins early 2000s in Dominica, style made more popular by producer Dada and ASA, hits Famalay and Conch Shell, also called Jump up soca.
# - Wikipedia via Music of Dominica text (search result, 2026-10-20): an older widely copied framing describes the bouyon soca term as coined by non-Dominican producers, mainly from Saint Lucia. The two published framings do not agree with each other.
# - Showcase Your Music, artist biography published under the name Dada (opened 2026-10-20): self published artist bio used here with attribution only. Bushtown Clan circle, beatmaking at 15, Triple Kay International productions, Nursery Krew Inc songs Peanuts and Calaloo.
# - Ebuzztt, article on the Smoke Riddim (opened 2026-10-20): Dominican producer Dada, hybrid riddim blending soca and Dominica bouyon, Bunji Garlin and Shurwayne Winchester singles, Famalay and Conch Shell productions, Patrice Roberts and Nadia Batson credits.
# - YouTube official credits: Famalay, produced by DadaMuzic and DSM, mixed by DadaMuzic; Conch Shell, produced by Dadamanufakture, Skinny Fabulous recorded at Dadamanufakture in Dominica.
# Note: web sources publish a full name for Dada, but the site record does not carry one and Sean has not confirmed one for this site, so no full name is printed in this profile.

